Here are some highly asked Kubernetes questions with short recall answers you can keep handy 👇

⸻

🔹 Deployment vs StatefulSet
	•	Deployment → stateless, interchangeable pods.
	•	StatefulSet → stateful apps, stable ID + storage.

🔹 When use StatefulSet?
	•	Databases, Kafka, Zookeeper → need stable identity & ordered startup.

🔹 Volumes
	•	Deployment: shared/ephemeral PVCs.
	•	StatefulSet: unique PVC per pod.

🔹 Why StatefulSet pod fails in another AZ?
	•	PV is AZ-bound → can’t attach outside zone.

🔹 PV/PVC across zones
	•	Default: zone-specific (EBS, PD).
	•	Fix: multi-AZ storage (EFS, Portworx).

🔹 DaemonSet
	•	Ensures 1 pod per node → logging, monitoring, networking.

🔹 Want 2 pods per node?
	•	Use Deployment/StatefulSet with affinity rules (DaemonSet can’t do 2 per node).

🔹 Pod Disruption Budget (PDB)
	•	Ensures min pods stay up during voluntary disruptions (node drain/upgrade).

🔹 Cert rotation (on-prem)
	•	kubeadm cert renew or cert-manager + automation.

🔹 Multi-AZ challenges
	•	Storage constraints, cross-AZ latency/costs, affinity misconfigs.

🔹 Scheduler logic
	•	Filter → Score → Bind (resources, affinity, taints).

🔹 StatefulSet pod volume issue
	•	Pod stuck if volume is in another AZ → fix with multi-AZ storage or same-zone scheduling.
